      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Vietnam generally offers a mature, English-proficient business culture with established chemical supply chains that favor long-term partnerships and consistent reliability. In contrast, Nigeria faces more significant logistical challenges, including infrastructure limitations and political instability, which can disrupt sourcing schedules despite a growing market for local manufacturing. While Nigerian suppliers can offer cost advantages and faster navigance of local regulations, the higher risk profile often requires stricter quality control and contingency planning compared to the more predictable environment in Vietnam. Ultimately, your decision will depend on whether you prioritize cost and speed in a complex region or stability and established processes in a developed one.",
